  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Discussion",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Use the `advancedCommerceInfo` object to indicate the message to display and the signed request.",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Before using this object to provide a custom offer or switch-plan recommendation, ensure that the app has a default message that you’ve assigned to its generic product identifiers. For more information on setting up generic product identifiers, see Set up generic product identifiers in `setting-up-your-project-for-advanced-commerce`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AdvancedCommerceAPI/setting-up-your-project-for-advanced-commerce"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "> **Note**\n>\n> Providing `advancedCommerceInfo` isn’t available for subscription bundles; respond with a `message` instead.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/message"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If you don’t have access to the Advanced Commerce API (ACA), use the `alternateProduct` or `promotionalOffer` keys of the `RealtimeResponseBody`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.retentionmessaging/documentation/RetentionMessaging/RealtimeResponseBody"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For more information, see `AdvancedCommerceAPI`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AdvancedCommerceAPI"
          ]
        }
      ],
